{"type":"assistant","message":{"type":"message","model":"newapi/gemini-3.8-flash-high","usage":{"input_tokens":8789,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"claude_cache_creation_5_m_tokens":0,"claude_cache_creation_1_h_tokens":0},"role":"assistant","id":"nSfnapSUKZjb1e8P34eHeQ","content":[{"signature":"","thinking":"The request is for \"web-design-guidelines\" and the command name is also specified as \"/web-design-guidelines\". The project is authorized as an isolated acceptance project with read-only/execution scope. It's forbidden to install skills, dependencies or browser. Modification to other projects, submissions, pushes, or external transmissions are disallowed. Verify actual validation and uncovered areas. Skill recommendations cannot substitute current project facts.\n\n\nAnalyzing `src/index.html` to assess keyboard accessibility according to local guidelines, focusing on menu interactions. Evaluating code against established keyboard navigation conventions, looking for potential mismatches or areas needing improvement. The primary concern is ensuring logical focus order and proper handling of keyboard events within the menu structure.\n\nThe \"open menu\" `div` lacks keyboard focusability because it lacks a `tabindex` or is not a native focusable element, preventing keyboard users from interacting with it via Tab key. This violates keyboard accessibility guidelines mandating keyboard event handlers for interactive elements. The correct implementation uses semantic HTML, like a `<button>`, rather than a `div` with an `onclick` event. This will correctly handle keyboard navigation (Tab) and activation (Enter/Space) and ensure keyboard users can open the menu.\n\n\nThe menu's initial state lacks several crucial accessibility features: focus isn't moved into the `<nav>`, nor is there an escape mechanism.  Essential ARIA attributes like `aria-expanded` and `aria-controls` are missing. The disclosure pattern should be adopted using a `<button>` trigger with `aria-expanded` and sequential tab navigation. Without any focus styles, it's impossible to ensure visible focus across browsers. These findings require detailed examination of the code and how it works.\n\n\nThe project's isolated environment prevents real-browser accessibility testing, such as using Chrome DevTools or screen readers, due to restrictions against installing browsers.  The analysis will be based on code review, focusing on keyboard navigation and ARIA attributes according to the provided guidelines.\n\nThe menu trigger, using a `div` element with an `onclick` event, lacks keyboard focus and event handling, violating keyboard accessibility principles.  This element requires updating to use a semantic HTML element like `<button>` to ensure proper keyboard interaction. The correct implementation is `<button>Open Menu</button>`.\n\n\nThe initial `div` acting as a menu trigger is not natively focusable; therefore, keyboard interaction is impossible. Replacing it with a `<button>` ensures keyboard focus and activation via Enter/Space. The absence of a toggle mechanism and `aria-expanded` and `aria-controls` attributes on the menu trigger prevents assistive technologies from conveying the menu's state (open/closed). Implementing a toggle mechanism with these attributes, including an \"escape\" key to close the menu, will resolve these issues.\n\n\n","type":"thinking"}],"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a35d2dea-0412-4e6a-b279-88a032851a30","uuid":"6efb5f28-91e5-4060-b1fd-e9fefc7aaa2b","timestamp":"2026-11-01T11:51:12.826Z","thinking_duration_ms":12010,"thinking_display":"updates"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"type":"message","model":"newapi/gemini-3.8-flash-high","usage":{"input_tokens":8789,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"claude_cache_creation_5_m_tokens":0,"claude_cache_creation_1_h_tokens":0},"role":"assistant","id":"nSfnapSUKZjb1e8P34eHeQ","content":[{"type":"text","text":"基于本地规则 snapshot（`web-interface-guidelines.md`）与 `src/index.html` 源码，对菜单的键盘可访问性审查结果如下：\n\n---\n\n### 🔍 审查发现 (Static Findings)\n\n#### 1. 菜单触发器使用 `<div>` 且缺失键盘聚焦与事件\n- **位置**：`src/index.html:1`\n  ```html\n  <div onclick=\"document.querySelector('nav').hidden=false\">打开菜单</div>\n  ```\n- **适用规则**：\n  - `<button> for actions, <a>/<Link> for navigation (not <div onClick>)`\n  - `Interactive elements need keyboard handlers (onKeyDown/onKeyUp)`\n  - `Use semantic HTML (<button>, <a>, <label>, <table>) before ARIA`\n  - 反模式：`<div> or <span> with click handlers (should be <button>)`\n- **源码事实**：使用非交互元素 `<div>` 挂载 `onclick`，未设置 `tabindex=\"0\"`，无键盘监听。\n- **触发条件**：用户使用 `Tab` 键在页面内导航，或尝试按 `Enter` / `Space` 键触发。\n- **后果**：键盘焦点无法落在“打开菜单”上，键盘用户完全无法触发打开操作；屏幕阅读器无法将其识别为按钮。\n- **修正建议**：将 `<div>` 替换为原生 `<button type=\"button\">`，天然获得 `Tab` 聚焦及 `Enter` / `Space` 激活能力。\n\n---\n\n#### 2. 状态未对辅助技术暴露且缺少键盘收起机制\n- **位置**：`src/index.html:1`\n  ```html\n  <div onclick=\"document.querySelector('nav').hidden=false\">打开菜单</div>\n  <nav hidden><a href=\"#content\">内容</a></nav>\n  ```\n- **交互契约**：Disclosure（折叠展开）模式\n- **源码事实**：仅单向设置 `nav.hidden = false`；缺少开闭状态标识及关联绑定。\n- **触发条件**：屏幕阅读器聚焦触发器；用户展开后需要收起菜单。\n- **后果**：\n  - 读屏软件无法感知菜单当前的折叠/展开状态。\n  - 键盘用户打开后无快捷收起路径（单向展开）。\n- **修正建议**：\n  - 在触发按钮上增加 `aria-expanded=\"false\"` 和 `aria-controls=\"menu-nav\"`。\n  - 切换时同步更新 `aria-expanded` 与 `hidden` 属性。\n\n---\n\n#### 3. 增强建议（条件推荐）\n- **分类**：条件性增强（遵循 Disclosure 模式，避免过度设计为 ARIA `role=\"menu\"`）\n- **建议**：\n  - **Escape 键关闭**：在展开状态下，监听 `Escape` 键关闭 `<nav>` 并将焦点移回打开按钮。\n  - **可见焦点指示器**：当前无样式表，依赖用户代理默认外观；建议添加显式的 `:focus-visible` 焦点样式（规则：`Interactive elements need visible focus: focus-visible:ring-* or equivalent`）。\n\n---\n\n### 🛠️ 建议修正方案\n\n```html\n<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"zh\">\n<head>\n  <title>菜单</title>\n</head>\n<body>\n  <button\n    type=\"button\"\n    id=\"menu-btn\"\n    aria-expanded=\"false\"\n    aria-controls=\"menu-nav\"\n    onclick=\"\n      const nav = document.getElementById('menu-nav');\n      const expanded = this.getAttribute('aria-expanded') === 'true';\n      this.setAttribute('aria-expanded', !expanded);\n      nav.hidden = expanded;\n    \"\n  >打开菜单</button>\n\n  <nav id=\"menu-nav\" hidden>\n    <a href=\"#content\">内容</a>\n  </nav>\n\n  <main id=\"content\">首页</main>\n</body>\n</html>\n```\n\n---\n\n### ⚠️ 未验证项说明 (Unverified Scope)\n\n- **未覆盖项**：\n  1. 真实浏览器环境下的默认焦点环（Focus Ring）高亮渲染与视觉对比度表现。\n  2. 真实屏幕阅读器（如 macOS VoiceOver、NVDA）对状态变更事件的实际朗读行为。\n- **限制说明**：\n  - 本次为纯静态源码及本地规则审查。依据项目 `CLAUDE.md` 约束（*“遵守任务的只读/实施范围；不安装技能、依赖或浏览器”*），当前环境禁止安装浏览器与相关测试依赖，故未在真实运行时中执行端到端交互验证。"}],"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a35d2dea-0412-4e6a-b279-88a032851a30","uuid":"c6f40b5c-e3b7-4b82-98d2-2488c26f1dd4","timestamp":"2026-11-01T11:51:19.389Z"}
